### kernel view of the line ###

   87:          0  msmgpio  72 Edge      wcd9320

  The parent is msmgpio 72, edge triggered, zero assertions.


### verdict against the interpretation table ###

  raw line low        : yes, at setup and in all 45 samples
  status clear        : yes, 00 00 00 00 throughout
  no IRQ              : yes, count 0, spurious 0, acked 0
  -> "clean idle pass" row


### the one deviation: MASK2 ###

  written  ff ff ff 7f
  read     ff ff 3f 7f
                 ^^ bits 6-7 of MASK2 did not take

  MASK2 bits 6-7 are IRQ 22 and 23, WCD9XXX_IRQ_RESERVED_0/1. They are
  read-only zero on this silicon and cannot be masked. 45 samples confirm the
  corresponding status bits never assert, so there is nothing behind them.

  MASK3 bit 6 -- IRQ 30, VBAT_MONITOR_RELEASE, the one real source left
  unmasked by the reset state -- DID take: 0x3f became 0x7f. That was the
  actual safety concern from the topology survey and it is resolved.

  Fixed by writing the achievable value ff ff 3f 7f, so the readback check
  stays meaningful instead of reporting an expected mismatch forever.


### suspend / resume ###

  Two real s2idle cycles:
    [ 126.148] Restarting tasks: Done / PM: suspend exit
    [ 661.827] PM: suspend entry (s2idle)
    [ 673.149] Restarting tasks: Done / PM: suspend exit

  After resume, at uptime 1093 s:
    identity  major 0x0102 minor 0x0001 laddr 0xcb up 1 down 0   (unchanged)
    irq line  87: 0 msmgpio 72 Edge wcd9320                      (still zero)
    masks     0x094=ff 0x095=ff 0x096=3f 0x097=7f                (preserved)
    status    0x098..0x09b = 00 00 00 00                         (clear)
    adsp      running
    slim errors 0, timeouts 0

  The SSH session dies across suspend because the USB gadget network drops.
  That is expected and is not a fault; uptime confirms no reboot occurred.


