### noted, not caused by this change ###

  [56.9-58.8] rcu: INFO: rcu_preempt detected expedited stalls on CPUs/tasks

  The same stall appeared at the same point in the previous boot, which was
  running the OLD driver (dual-rc1) with no interrupt code at all. So it is
  pre-existing and unrelated. It did not distort the sampling window: the
  fast phase ran 47.8 -> 54.2 s for 20 samples and the slow phase 54.2 ->
  79.8 s for 25, both essentially on schedule.
